Clearwave — model-free local packages

Launch “Clearwave” from the application menu, or run clearwave.
Opening the window does not start microphone capture.

The .deb packages contain the same amd64 executable, built against Ubuntu 24.04
libraries. They target Debian 13, Ubuntu 24.04 or newer, and Linux Mint 22.x.
An AMD GPU with a working Vulkan driver and an active PipeWire session is required
for live denoising. No system service is installed or enabled by this package.

No NVIDIA installer, model, DLL, or exported weights are included. Choose your
locally supplied extracted model folder in Settings. Files must be obtained and
used under terms applicable to you. Packaging does not resolve model-use rights.

For /usr/bin installations, settings and optional local runtime assets use:
  ${XDG_DATA_HOME:-$HOME/.local/share}/clearwave/runtime/
The settings file is desktop.json; an automatically detected bundle uses vendor/.
Removing the package preserves this per-user directory.

For manual CLI extraction, install 7zip, then use “clearwave --help”.

Clearwave’s original code is MIT licensed; see LICENSE. For legal reasons,
NVIDIA model files are not distributed. Obtain NVIDIA RTX Voice separately.

For DLL-free processing, select a folder containing voice-weights.safetensors
or model.safetensors. The original encrypted model plus NVAudioEffects.dll can
also be together in the selected folder, or in their original NvAFX subfolders.
